{"content":[{"c":["KIBROTH-HATTAAVAH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Location in the wilderness where the Israelites who were killed by plague for craving meat from Egypt were buried (",{"href":"?bref=Num.11.34-35","r":"Num.11.34-35","rawR":"Num.11.34-35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.11.34-35","value":"Num.11.34-35"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 11:34-35"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.33.16-17","r":"Num.33.16-17","rawR":"Num.33.16-17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.33.16-17","value":"Num.33.16-17"}],"t":"ref","v":"33:16-17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.9.22","r":"Deut.9.22","rawR":"Deut.9.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.9.22","value":"Deut.9.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 9:22"},"). It was situated between Mt Sinai and Hazeroth, but its exact site is unknown. The name, meaning “graves of craving,” accords with the account of the quails."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=WildernessWanderings_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"WildernessWanderings_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"WildernessWanderings_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Wilderness Wanderings"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"KibrothHattaavah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Nm 11:34-35","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.11.34-35","rawQueryValue":"Num.11.34-35","sourceRefExact":"Num.11.34-35"},{"anchorText":"33:16-17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.33.16-17","rawQueryValue":"Num.33.16-17","sourceRefExact":"Num.33.16-17"},{"anchorText":"Dt 9:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.9.22","rawQueryValue":"Deut.9.22","sourceRefExact":"Deut.9.22"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"8c3eb86f8a484300dcb824515ae66d0252fba38